&lt;p&gt;US President Donald Trump will raise the issue of nuclear arms reduction during an unprecedented meeting with Russian President Vladimir Putin and Chinese President Xi Jinping in China next week, the White House said on Friday. The three leaders are expected to meet on Thursday on the sidelines of the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) forum in Shenzhen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;White House spokeswoman Olivia Wales said Trump believes the proliferation of nuclear weapons poses a serious danger and wants to discuss reducing global nuclear stockpiles. The meeting will be part of Trump's four-day Asian tour, which begins on Monday and also includes a visit to the Philippines.&lt;/p&gt;
